{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q409202","formula":"CHO₃⁻","hill":"CHO3","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":1.0,"H":1.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"Bicarbonate ion","ru":"Гидрокарбонаты","uk":"Гідрокарбонати"},"descriptions":{"en":"In inorganic chemistry, bicarbonate (American English: ; IUPAC-recommended nomenclature: hydrogencarbonate) is an intermediate form in the deprotonation of carbonic acid. It is a polyatomic anion with the chemical formula HCO3–. Bicarbonate serves a crucial biochemical role in the physiological pH buffering system.","ru":"Гидрокарбона́ты — кислые соли угольной кислоты H2CO3. Формула аниона: HCO−3. Устаревшие названия гидрокарбонатов: кислый, углекислый, двууглекислый, бикарбонаты.","uk":"Гі́дрокарбона́ти (застаріла назва — бікарбонати) — кислі солі карбонатної кислоти H2CO3 (містять аніон HCO-3). Наприклад, до гідрокарбонатів належить питна сода NaHCO3. Гідрокарбонати, на відміну від карбонатів, у воді розчинні."},"fame":53,"pubchemCid":769,"mass":61.017,"charge":-1,"smiles":"C(=O)(O)[O-]","inchikey":"BVKZGUZCCUSVTD-UHFFFAOYSA-M","iupac":"hydrogen carbonate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"769","atoms":5,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.39,"y":-0.21,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.923,"y":-0.989,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.521,"y":1.191,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":0.054,"y":0.008,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":1.873,"y":0.644,"z":0.0,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,3,1],[0,4,1],[1,3,1],[2,3,2]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q409202","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bicarbonate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%93%D0%B8%D0%B4%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BA%D0